! The porch ~ the sweeper's kit

The operator ruled on 2026-10-26 to close open work before the founding bake. This lane sweeps the road's hygiene pile (burned-name guards, evergreen remainders, tests-only debts, re-measures and canon sweeps) beside the slotted lanes, in small trains: each bundle lands off the span head, and the controller writes the road at each land. The crew stands as <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes">>: one builder, one reader who surveys the bundle and reads each commit, the lead running every suite.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-one>>

!! Bundle one ~ three tooling items and the burned-name guards

!!! The Playwright engine cache
* ''A CDN stall once held a runner for 20 minutes and for 48.'' Every job in `.github/workflows` that installs engines (`ci.yml`'s browser-vessel suite, floor crossing and standalone single-file suite; `held-out.yml`'s browser-weld cell) now restores `~/.cache/ms-playwright` keyed on the runner OS, the Playwright version `pnpm exec playwright --version` names, and the engine set. The install step still runs for the system libraries and downloads only on a miss. A version bump re-downloads once.
* ''Stays.'' The TiddlyWiki5 submodule's own `bin/ci-test.sh` installs engines for upstream's CI, outside this repository's workflows.

!!! The household witness image
* ''`household-https-witness` builds `lares-surface:local` from this tree on every run'' when `HOUSEHOLD_IMAGE` stands unset, so a stale local tag never meets newer code (the layer cache keeps an unchanged tree cheap). A set `HOUSEHOLD_IMAGE` reads as given and builds only when the tag stands absent.
* `tools/harbor-walk-witness.sh` holds the same line with `HARBOR_IMAGE` (#/bundle-two).

!!! The `custody-frames` U1 leak
* ''The cause.'' U1's control read `loadActivePersonaIndex().catch(() => undefined)`. That reader infers the one face standing open, and it opens the seated custody, which refuses outside a scratch root. Under a real `HOME` the refusal fell into the `catch` and the assertion read green by accident; under a scratch `HOME` or `LAR_ROOT` the custody opened, an earlier vector's face stood open, and the reader answered `0`.
* ''The cure.'' The control reads the composition's own choice (`mountedFaceOrdinal()`), the thing the unlock frame sets, and the file reads green under a real `HOME` and under a scratch `HOME` with a scratch `LAR_ROOT`. The test title no longer claims a case it never asserted: an unlock naming no face mounts the vessel's one face by the door's own rule.

!!! Burned-name guards burned
* `lar-wire.test.ts`: the control that `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` pass no door (road `F8`).
* `browser-walk.test.ts`: the control that the `boot-invite-burned`, `hosting-walk` and `nexus-keys` stores stand absent (road `W20`).
* `vessel-wipe-surfaces.test.ts`, now `vessel-surfaces.test.ts`: the `vessel clear`, `rite rebirth` and `--clear` refusals and the negative help checks; the live `read`, refresh and surface-table assertions stay.
* `nexus-verb-reach.test.ts`: `nexus refresh` reads as an unknown verb.
* `vault-door.test.ts`: the former vault verbs (`seal`, `rotate`, `repair`, `passphrase`, `export`), `--yes`, `--check` and the passphrase environment route; the exact seven-verb help assertion and a nonsense-verb refusal stay.
* `cabal-realm-ceremony.test.ts`: the absent-export list for the former eviction and closing API; the exact live export assertion stays.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-two>>

!! Bundle two ~ the stream manifest, the witness image, the leak and the readings

!!! Closed
* ''`G38` The stream manifest stands as one shape in both languages.'' The Python writer (`sensorium.py`) declares `lifecycle` in every stream manifest: it mirrors `deriveLifecycle` at mint, `set_stream_ephemeral` recomputes it when `ephemeral` flips, and a declared `tombstone` stays. The reader (`sensorium.ts`) requires a declared state and refuses an absent one by name; the derivation fallback burned. The builder keeps its mint-time default, which writes the field. Python tests pin the writer and the setter; the node tests pin the refusal beside its control.
* ''`tools/harbor-walk-witness.sh` builds from the tree'' with `HARBOR_IMAGE` unset, as the household witness does.
* ''The `held-out-steps` test names its actor.'' The plan test read `git config user.name`, which a scratch `HOME` lacks; it now names `GITHUB_ACTOR` as the runner does, and the file reads green under a scratch `HOME`.

!!! Readings, no change owed
* ''`H7`.'' No line in `membership-doctrine` calls an introduction's lifetime unruled any longer. `#/the-invite` states that the answer consumes the introduction, that the three dials count and read no clock, and that a posture names a setting and never a date. The strike belongs to the road.
* ''`G19` carriers read true against the code at this head.'' The five sweeps met no disagreeing line:
** `docker-compose.mesh.yml` and `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml` both state that the localhost exemption is not TLS and cite each other;
** `secure-context#/behind-the-terminator` and `harbor#/household-https` agree on `LAR_PUBLIC_URL`, loopback publication and the scheme;
** the test door's marker (`.lar-test-scratch`) and the suites' temp-dir check (`scratch-custody-setup.ts`) stand as two named things, and no carrier merges them.
* ''`kahu.mem` and `lamplighters.mem` on what the code holds'' needs a reader who holds the operator's intent for the cadence share. It stays on `G19` for the controller.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-three>>

!! Bundle three ~ the harness image, the marker test, the flush reading and the carried items

!!! Closed
* ''`A9` The browser harness stands as an image.'' `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml`'s `qa` runner builds the `browser-harness` Dockerfile target: the pinned Playwright client, the two browser walks (`browser-ci-smoke.mjs`, `live-wiki.mjs`), their join helper and the built custody probe, and no repository bind (the `/exchange` bind and the tmpfs stay). `tools/browser-ci.sh` builds the image when absent. `harness-image-law` scans the `qa` service and the target, with the old bind planted as its red control; the mesh's `browser-a` and `browser-b` stay its two named exceptions. The target built and ran on this host: Playwright imports in the image, and the walks and probe sit where the walks look for them.
* ''`G17` The node daemon's scratch marker admits nothing.'' Canon rules it (`harbor` (the container boundary and the test custody door)): every boot rests at the floor holding no vessel key, and a harness opens a staged vessel through the test custody door alone. `test-scratch-marker-admission.test.ts` pins that a marked root yields the TEST SCRATCH notice, an unmarked root yields none, and after the notice the seated holder stays locked and a sealed row refuses at the floor. `main.ts` calls the extracted `testScratchNotice`.
* ''`G8` The per-verb flush stands measured, and its instrument is `tools/flush-bench.mjs`.'' A verb ends at its awaited `flush([document])`; the bench times that call as a microbenchmark, a one-field change to a synthetic document in a `Repo` over the product's store adapter (`DurableNodeFSStorageAdapter`), and dispatches no product verb. One reading, 2026-10-27, Node 24, the 443 carriers under `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba` resident as 443 documents: per-verb flush p50 5.7 ms, p95 8.2 ms, p99 11.7 ms, max 13.5 ms (n = 443); the one-document control reads p50 4.5 ms, p95 6.3 ms (n = 100). The whole-repo `flush()` that names no document reads p50 15.6 ms, p95 24.5 ms (n = 20). So a verb that names its document pays about a millisecond over the control at full corpus, and a flush that names none pays about three times that. The first flush of the loaded corpus took 0.9 s. A planted-set test (`flush-bench.test.mjs`) reads the arithmetic before any reading trusts it, and the bench refuses a corpus under 400 carriers.
* ''`G20` the sensorium `requirements.txt` tree-sitter pins.'' The binding pin (`tree-sitter==0.26.0`) is the newest the index holds; the carrier grammar generates ABI 15, inside the binding's 13 to 15 window. `test_tree_sitter_pins.py` holds that pair to the tree, with a planted out-of-window control, and the pin equals the installed binding.
* ''`G20` the Elyncia carrier that failed the corpus round-trip.'' At this head the round-trip law holds for every carrier under `bags/`. `meme-corpus-roundtrip.test.ts` now sweeps all of `bags/` (the six bags, 778 carriers) in place of the lares bag alone, and a second test fails by name on any carrier the law skips by shape. The carrier is no longer unowned: the standing law owns it.
* The sensorium conftest exempts `ANONYMIZED_TELEMETRY` as the third-party one-shot the mempalace package stamps on first import. Whichever test imported it first used to carry the blame.

!!! Stays, with its reason
* ''`G20` the cold-boot `unavailable` reading.'' The per-source map reads as follows. `findWithProgress` (automerge-repo 2.6.0-alpha.5, `DocumentQuery`) answers `unavailable` once no source is pending and the handle holds no data, and the state carries a `sources` map (`storage`, `automerge-sync`). A hearth-private doc has no peer to wait on, so `unavailable` reads terminal; the one case it misreads is a write this vessel has issued and not yet rested. `boot-resolver.ts` covers that case with a two-second grace on a monotonic clock. A clock decides there, which the house law forbids, and the cure is the writer's own event: the caller names the flush it owes (`repo.flush([id])`) and the resolver asks again after it settles. The production caller that needs it is `open-node-vessel.ts` (`readDaemonDoc`), K15's file, and `K15`'s bonds (PR #106) built that cure: `resolveBootDoc` takes an optional `settled`, `readDaemonDoc` passes the Repo's flush, and `UNAVAILABLE_GRACE_MS` retired.
* ''`G8` pack-PIN recursion and the `assertBodyIndexTier` caller.'' Pack-PIN recursion stays unbuilt (`blob-carriage#/proposed-law`); the tier caller arrives with the cad body-index writer, since `bodyIndexBagUri` has no producer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-five>>

!! Bundle five ~ the workflow law, the walk image, the evergreen instrument and the road's true-up

!!! Closed
* ''Every workflow job carries `timeout-minutes`, and every Playwright install its own.'' A capless job ran under the runner's 360-minute default. Each cap clears the slowest of the last ten green runs with margin (Test 100 against a 71-minute green, Witnesses 40, an e2e shard 50), and the one-minute jobs carry 10 to 20; each `playwright install` step carries ten minutes after an engine cache whose key names the Playwright version, and that step cap catches a stalled CDN. A reusable-workflow call (`ci.yml`'s `e2e`) takes none, since its called jobs carry their own. `tools/workflow-law.test.mjs` reads every workflow and fails by job and step name, with a planted capless workflow as its control.
* ''`tools/browser-ci.sh` builds the walk image from the tree on every `qa` run'' with `BROWSER_CI_HARNESS_IMAGE` unset; a named tag reads as given and builds only when absent. The image bakes the walks, so a standing default tag ran an older tree's walk bytes. `browser-ci.test.mjs` plants a standing tag as the red and pins the build before the run, and a text pin holds `household-https-witness.sh` and `harbor-walk-witness.sh` to their build-from-tree gate.
* ''`tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` reads three more shapes.'' A comment that names its lane, wave or slice (`Wave C`, `slice 2`, `this lane`) reads as narration; the `#` comments of the workflows, the Dockerfile and the root compose files join the narration corpus; `canon-dated-history` counts a verb of history within 40 characters of an ISO date in live canon, and a date with a ruling or correction marker (`RULED`, `ruled`, `ruling`, `CORRECTION`, `CORRECTED`) within 40 characters carries provenance and reads nothing. Each carries a planted red and a lawful control in the self-test.
* ''The finds stand cured'' outside the fenced files: the source, tool and workflow comments, and fourteen live-canon carriers that dated a landing or a burn (two dated corrections stay as provenance). The node identity header names five sealed rows and no selector; the Kahu realm's group seam names its road row `P21`.
* ''The road's true-up'' rides its own commits, one concern each, named in the lane's hand-back.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bundle-six>>

!! Bundle six ~ the old shapes and the shape gates burn

Operator, 2026-10-28: the old shapes and shape gates are design-time crud that teaches agents to repeat the pattern; early alpha holds, a cut re-founds and never recognises old bytes, and the boundary guards get designed fresh after the founding.

!!! Closed
* ''The free recognisers burn.'' The `LARK` old-shape readings of the S and FCK envelopes, the sealed writer's refusal of them, the KEL `old-shape-inception` producer, and the capture cell's retired `feedback` spelling (`build-patch.ts`, `turn-harvest.ts`, and `move-skeleton.ts`, which the census missed) leave source. Those bytes fall to the generic `bare`, `torn` or `malformed` readings, which stay. The tests that proved only the old shapes burn; every wrong-key, torn, bare and foreign-family test stays.
* ''`tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` reads a fifth class, `old-shape`'': a `Legacy*Refus*` or `OldShape*` identifier, the `"old-shape"` literal, and a comment that names a retired shape. Its ceiling reads 0 and no exception stands.
* ''The roster'' (the Terra builds, the Sol reads) and the crew law's seven refinements stand in `mixed-model-swarm`.

!!! Slice two ~ closed
* ''The store-acknowledgement race was the product's.'' A daemon island's `doc:rest` ask rides `parentPort` and outruns the island's sync handshake, so the vessel's `repo.find` of a document the island had just minted read `unavailable` before the Repo had met the island's peer. `DaemonVmCore.syncLegReady()` names the leg the island runs on (the first leg and each manifest-replay leg), the rest door awaits it through a removable teardown subscription, and an `unavailable` after the leg stands still rejects. No clock, no retry loop. The pins are D6 to D8 in `rest-door.test.ts`; the replay probe fixture (`daemon-replay-probe.mjs`) stands for the island and waits on the Repo's own `peer` event the same way.
* ''The wiki-shore family flaked in the tests.'' They counted host turns after a store write, while the store closes a change with a changeset on a later tick; under load that changeset landed after the next step, re-owed hands and flushed marked ones. The rig's `arrived()` now waits on the changeset event, and `landingIdle()` follows where a landing is wanted. The product holds no race there.
* ''The 23 fenced old-shape sites burned in one commit with their exceptions'': the browser legacy-archive and old veil-row refusals, the keyhive legacy face-signature refusal (a place-signed edge now stops at the Binding Gate) and the `placeVerifyingKey` input only it read, the node legacy place-bytes refusal, and the `old-shape-inception` member of `PlaceKelRefusal` with its node mappings and the `old-shape` reading. The class stands at 0 with none excepted.
* ''LARK-led bytes read `bare`, and the tests say so.'' A LARK-led file at a listed carrier refuses a founding and a carrier write as `bare` and leaves the store untouched. The law of the unlisted path: a bare file at a path no listed carrier names does not block a founding, because it is not custody's; only a file bearing the seal's magic (`sealed`, `torn`) does. The operator ratified this: custody claims only what it names, per the old-shapes ruling.
* ''The retired `focus=` and `feedback` spellings stand as nothing'': the harvester fixtures write `aperture=`, a `feedback=` key reads as an unknown key that closes nothing, and a `focus` or `feedback` head reads as water.
* ''`tools/launch-copilot.mjs` refuses any model id naming fusion'' in both modes: Fusion integration waits until after the founding, and a router with a hidden lineage cannot serve as a named lens.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-stays>>

!! What stays, and why

* ''The CLI unknown-command list and the keyhive cabal names (road `W20`).'' The unknown-command refusal is generic and tests with a nonsense control; no named cabal guard remains outside the held modules (`ceremony-core.ts`, `keyhive-provider.ts`, `boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`, K15).
* ''Bundle four stands unbuilt'' for a fresh crew. Four designs, each with where its ruling lives and its first reading:
** ''`G6` outside the two vessel files'' (the road's `G6`, #/after-the-seat; the evergreen sweep's rulings at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026">>). Stale prose, back-compat wording and tolerant readers in `nexus-seal-seed.ts`, `seed-wrap-prf.ts`, `ingest-core.ts`, `lar-uris.ts` and `mesh-palace.ts`; `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` wait for K15; `cleanup-days.ts` stays unlocated. Instrument: `node tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` and its EXCEPTIONS (each names its owner). Check each file against the live lanes before editing.
** ''Road (iv) surfaces its impact set as information, ruled 2026-10-27'' (the road's `G20`, #/stride-2-floor). On a quorum-membership change, derive from the board records which admits and offices leaned on a departed signer and surface that impact set for review as information. Nothing cascades; a quorum revokes by name on the deny board. Canon: `lamplighters.mem` near line 205 and `kahu.mem` lines 431 to 437. First read: the board readers, the seat-change and roll path, where a departed signer is known, and where a reviewer reads the set (a CLI command, a verb or a field on an existing status). Size it before building; write a lane brief if it passes a bundle.
** ''Loans keyed by CID after a causal expiry, ruled 2026-10-27'' (the road's `G20`, #/stride-2-floor). A loan keys by CID and keeps its holder and tier, once it carries a causal expiry counted in rolls or epochs (`blob-carriage#/proposed-law` counts a grace in realm rolls). `effect-record.ts` lists `loan` TTL-pending; `residency-model.mem` line 154 defines the loan. The expiry comes first, and a clock never decides it. Write a lane brief if the expiry design passes a bundle.
** ''`/cas` verifies the body before the index names it, ruled 2026-10-27'' (the road's `G20`, #/stride-2-floor). The body lands and verifies before the public index names it. `bulb-read-face.ts` serves `/cas` after `publicCas.isPublic(cid)`. First read: every writer that lands a body and names it in the public index (`publicCas`, `content-handle.ts`, `bodyIndexBagUri`, which has no production producer today), then where the ordering is enforced and a red test that names a CID before its body verified.
* ''Also left.'' `G8` pack-PIN recursion and the `assertBodyIndexTier` caller (it arrives with the cad body-index writer); the K15-held `W20` names; the parallel-draft alert (hands room); the `kahu.mem` and `lamplighters.mem` sweep on `G19` (needs the operator's cadence-share intent); the `harness-image-law` and flush-bench instruments stay as built.
* ''Held out of bundle five, each for its owner.''
** The staged-only e2e vectors read SKIPPED outside staged mode, never green (PR #113): 43 test bodies under `describe.skipIf(!stagedTarget)`, and `tools/e2e-harness-law.test.mjs` reads red on the vacuous guard. Its scanner's gaps stay owed: a guard after a first statement, a multi-line `if`, `test.each` forms.
** `ingest-tolerant.ts` stays: it skips a torn cap event, a live fault, and names no retired shape.
** The one-shot corpus tools (`quote-named-params.mjs`, `quote-positionals.mjs`, `ranks-to-scale.mjs`, `photocopies-to-has.mjs`, `render-verify.mjs`, `bounded-reach-consistency.mjs`, `mesh-found-lararium.sh`) have no workflow caller, and none reads confirmed dead: `ranks-to-scale.mjs` still meets one `<<~ranks` carrier (`agent-worldline.mem`), `carrier-files.test.ts` names `photocopies-to-has.mjs`, and the quote, render and bounded-reach tools serve as repair or design instruments. Each burns after a reader confirms its target gone.
** Two narration finds sit in the hands spine's files: `open-browser-vessel.ts` (`W26 slice 5`) and `open-node-vessel.ts` (`Slice 2`). The ceiling counts them until that owner touches the lines.
** The rowless bullets of the road's `#/after-the-seat` (the boot order's four reds, wikis-first writes, the browser shore's worn face plane, fleet gathering's batch, the SES or Compartment realm gate, operator power over a browser vessel, observer-local hardening's bound, the bag-tier reader, the declared tier's share gate, the in-VM startup module) take ids in the next porch bundle.
** `epoch-binding-surfaces#/the-real-mover` records its own correction beside the error by design; its one dated line stays counted until its author rewrites the record.

<<~/ahu>>

